! mcp_bootstrap_p241.strap -- MCP printed page 241: the head of "THE
! OVERLAP INPUT PROGRAM FIXUPS" (RKA..RKH counts, R KS UK and the R W..
! rewind/retry entry RGWUK .. RWSTOR), lines 1-48.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.248, read at 400/600 dpi, 1200-2400
! dpi for doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11D11MCP  CARD ID CB000001  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 241";
! the heading row's LOCATION field is BLANK -- line 1 is a banner, as
! the workflow rule predicts.
!
! THE PAGE.  48 lines.  Lines 1-4 are comment cards (an asterisk banner
! "THE OVERLAP INPUT PROGRAM FIXUPS"; line 4 a bare "-").  Line 5
! "SLC,$" prints 227524.31 (with a "*" mark): printed p.240's last row
! is "R UNLD2 VF,0" at 227524.00 and a VF field is 25 bits, so the
! counter arrives at exactly 227524.31 -- this page JOINS p.240.  Lines
! 6-11 are six SYN cards (+00000000 NULL).  Lines 12-48 are located and
! contiguous from 227524.40 to 227551.40 (a half word; next location
! 227552.00, printed p.242's line 1).  Line 46 is a VF (227550.40,
! 25 bits; line 47 aligns to 227551.00).  No remarks are printed.
! Asterisks after the LOCATION on lines 5 and 30.
!
! LABEL SPELLINGS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 9 "RKC" = RKD: at 1200 dpi the third glyph has a straight
!     left stem and squared corners (worn D); line 8 is the real RKC.
!   * line 11 "RKF"/"RKH": at 2400 dpi the glyph has a left stem, a
!     middle bar and three faint dots where a right stem would be, and
!     no top bar -- H with its right stem worn (line 10 above prints a
!     clean F with a top bar).  Written RKH.  Nothing references it here.
!   * line 12 "RKS UK" = RKSUK, landed p.214 (B,RKSUK = 227524.40).
!   * line 15 "RUNLC" = RUNLD, line 22 "RGNOGC" = RGNOGD: D stems;
!     C22-6728 spells RUNLD (4x) and RGNOGD (3x).
!   * line 18 "Dw" = DW, line 23 "CWEF" = DWEF, line 46 "CBSP" = DBSP,
!     line 45 "DMCP": the landed p.104/p.108 D-names; KVI binaries
!     000001.77 / 000007.77 and VF 000006.00+ print exactly.
!   * line 26 "REJJCB" = REJJOB: C22-6728 spells REJJOB 28 times;
!     printed p.242 line 7 prints the O CLOSED (same 230364).
!   * line 33 "RCSWTC" = RDSWTC: C22-6728 "*RDSWTC" (2x); sibling RDSWBR.
!   * line 42 "RWTCNG" = RWTONG, line 43 "RWSTCR" = RWSTOR: open round,
!     written O as the p.242 transcription does (it defines RWTONG at
!     227554.40, which CBZ line 42 prints, and references RWSTOR at
!     227546.40, this page's line 43).  REJJOB on this page proves the
!     drum prints O open here.  Rests on ink plus p.242.
!   * line 47 "VSL(VU)" = VSU: U's right stem worn; p.242 lines 14/22
!     print LVE,,VSU(VU) with the same 000006.01 B3.
!   * hex bytes: "C1" (LVI), "C4" (KVI), "C0" (B, NOP, BZB h2) are 01,
!     04, 00, and line 40's SVA "C0" is D0 (worn D; p.233's SVA rows make
!     D0) -- each settled by what the statement assembles to.  BZXE
!     lines 24/30 print C0 and assemble C0: a real C.  Octal fields
!     "CCCCCC.CC" are 0; "3.C", "C.32" are 0.
!   * RGNOGD's value 230432.40 comes from BZB line 22's h2 .74 (an
!     address .00 prints .34, as line 34's RWSET-.32 shows).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials ?B000001 .. ?B000036 (prefix a round
! glyph; header prints "CB000001").  A new deck starts here.  Shared:
! 12/13 (012), 17/18 (016), 20/21 (018), 23/24 (020), 29/30 (025),
! 32/33 (027), 36/37 (030), 38/39 (031), 41/42 (033), 45-48 (036).
! No serial skipped on the page; printed p.242 opens at 038, so 037
! does not print on either page.

VU      SYN, $3                      ! p.213 line 25 "V U SYN,$3"
VSU     SYN, 6.0                     ! p.213 line 18 = VID.VH = 6.0
DMCP    SYN, 32.0                    ! landed p.108
DW      SYN, 1.32                    ! landed p.104 "D W"
DRD     SYN, 1.0                     ! landed p.104 "D RD"
DWEF    SYN, 7.32                    ! landed p.104 "D WEF"
DBSP    SYN, 6.0                     ! landed p.104 "D BSP"
RKSBRC  SYN, (8)230363.40            ! as p.214 writes it; LV line 12 230363.72 = .40 + 2x13, BIT-EXACT
RUNLD   SYN, (8)227502.0             ! BB line 15 h2, half word only
RDUK    SYN, (8)227757.0             ! BXE line 21, half word only
RGNOGD  SYN, (8)230432.40            ! BZB line 22 h2 .74 = .40 + .34 (BZB,..RWSET-.32 = .00 prints .34), half word only
RPUKLI  SYN, (8)230204.40            ! BZXE line 24 .72 (BZXE,RWEXBR .00 prints .32), half word only
REJJOB  SYN, (8)230364.0             ! BB line 26 REJJOB+.17 = 230364.21, BIT-EXACT (as p.242)
RWSET   SYN(BU,32,8), (8)227552.40   ! p.242 line 2 label of a half-word LVI; BB h2 .74, BZB RWSET-.32 = .34
RWTRY   SYN, (8)227643.40            ! LV line 27 .76 = .40 + 2x15, BIT-EXACT (OCR: RWTRY VF)
RETRY   SYN, (8)227643.0             ! V+ line 28 .36 = .00 + 2x15, BIT-EXACT (OCR: RETRY VF,RKC+1.0)
RWEXIT  SYN(BU,32), (8)227646.0             ! as p.219 writes it; LVI line 31 227646.37
RDSWBR  SYN, (8)230013.0             ! SIC line 32, BIT-EXACT
RDSWTC  SYN, (8)230007.0             ! B line 33, half word only
RWSBSP  SYN, (8)227556.0             ! LVI line 39 .37 = .00 + 31; p.242 line 8 label at 227556.00
RWTONG  SYN, (8)227554.40            ! CBZ line 42 .76; p.242 line 6 label at 227554.40
RETN    SYN, (8)230104.0             ! B line 48, half word only

